Sparsemap Release Notes
========================

Version 1.0.0 (2026-03-04)
--------------------------

Initial release with:
* Complete RLE (Run-Length Encoding) implementation
* Sparse bitmap encoding with 2-bit flags
* Efficient select() and scan() operations
* Comprehensive test suite
* Autoconf/Automake build system
* MIT License

Features:
* Sparse, compressed bitmap storage
* Best case: 2048 bits in 8 bytes
* Worst case: 2048 bits uncompressed + 8 bytes overhead
* RLE encoding for long runs of set bits
* O(1) select for RLE chunks
* Batch processing for scan operations

API:
* sparsemap_init()
* sparsemap_set()
* sparsemap_unset()
* sparsemap_is_set()
* sparsemap_select()
* sparsemap_scan()
* sparsemap_rank()
* sparsemap_count()
* And more...

For detailed documentation, see README.md and doc/RLE_IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md
